{
    desc => q{Ctrl-d scrolls viewport down by half a page},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/scrolling/ctrl_d_scroll`

Tests that `Ctrl-d` scrolls the viewport down by approximately half a page.
The buffer has 40 numbered lines so the half-page scroll is clearly visible.

Keys: `Ctrl-d`

- **ctrl_d_scroll_initial.png**: Cursor at line 1 col 0 on "scroll line 1".
- **ctrl_d_scroll_after_ctrl_d.png**: Viewport scrolled down ~half a page; cursor moved down accordingly.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-d');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_ctrl_d');
    },
}
